      "message": "You are effectively reducing the async space since when your hook rejects the request the reported error is \"no async space left\". I think it would be better to have a different error so someone diagnosing an issue can distinguish this from the normal out of space case.\n\nHow about putting this new hook after this conditional and return -EPERM, -EACCESS or something else. Then the new code is:\n```\ntrace_android_vh_binder_detect_low_async_space_locked(is_async, \u0026alloc-\u003efree_async_space, pid, \u0026should_fail);\nif (should_fail)\n  return ERR_PTR(-EPERM);\n```\nor if you might have multiple reasons for rejecting it, have the hook return the appropriate error:\n```\nint err \u003d 0;\ntrace_android_vh_binder_detect_low_async_space_locked(is_async, \u0026alloc-\u003efree_async_space, pid, \u0026err);\nif (err)\n  return ERR_PTR(err);\n```",
